Rule 2 (broadcastable shapes when ranks are equal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i) ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 3 (scalar-tensor broadcasting is allowed)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 4 (general NumPy-style broadcasting for different ranks)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : (shape(v_1, (ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) + j)) = shape(v_2, j) ∨ shape(v_1, (ndim(v_1) - ndim(v_2) + j)) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, j) = 1)) else (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 1) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_2, (ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) + j)) = shape(v_1, j) ∨ shape(v_2, (ndim(v_2) - ndim(v_1) + j)) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, j) = 1))
